# Hive of the Eye Tyrant's attack trigger still knows its defending player once Hive has left combat (CR 508.5: "If that
# creature is no longer attacking, the defending player it's referring to is the player that creature was attacking"). Bot2
# puts a Lotus Petal in its graveyard; Bot1 animates Hive and attacks Bot2, and the trigger targets the Petal (the only card
# there, so it is chosen without asking). Bot2 answers the trigger with a Lightning Bolt that kills the 3/3 Hive; the trigger
# resolves after Hive is gone, its target still legal, and the Petal is exiled (CR 608.2b).

[Bot1 Deck]
Hive of the Eye Tyrant
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Island x15

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain
Lotus Petal
Lightning Bolt
Island x15

